Match GUIX cross-compile behavior in libzmq.

GUIX builds bitcoin via a cross-toolchain (make-bitcoin-cross-toolchain
in contrib/guix/manifest.scm) even on native x86_64, so CMake sees
CMAKE_CROSSCOMPILING=TRUE when libzmq configures. libzmq's
CMakeLists.txt has TWO blocks gated by `if(NOT CMAKE_CROSSCOMPILING)`:

  Line 545: `if(ZMQ_HAVE_EVENTFD AND NOT CMAKE_CROSSCOMPILING)`
            -> zmq_check_efd_cloexec()
  Line 738: `if(NOT CMAKE_CROSSCOMPILING)`
            -> zmq_check_sock_cloexec()
            -> zmq_check_o_cloexec()
            -> zmq_check_so_bindtodevice()
            -> zmq_check_so_keepalive()
            -> zmq_check_so_priority()
            -> zmq_check_tcp_keep{cnt,idle,intvl,alive}()
            -> zmq_check_tcp_tipc()
            -> zmq_check_getrandom()

Each runs a small test program. Under cross-compile, all are skipped
and ALL ZMQ_HAVE_* macros stay undefined; under native compile they
all succeed (Nix sandbox has a real Linux kernel) and TCP/IP/IPC/
TIPC code paths get extra `#ifdef ZMQ_HAVE_*` branches.

Verified against GUIX's depends staging archives (extracted from
~b10c's GUIX build): tcp/ip/ipc_listener/tipc_* are the only members
of libzmq.a that differ between us and upstream. Force CMAKE_CROSSCOMPILING
TRUE right after project(ZeroMQ) so both blocks get skipped and all
ZMQ_HAVE_* macros stay undefined — matches GUIX.

Defensive ZMQ_HAVE_TIPC=FALSE before the source-list conditional
(the cross-compile branch already prevents it being set, but explicit
is clearer).

This patch is applied to libzmq 4.3.5 inside Bitcoin Core's depends/
sources, before the depends Makefile runs its own patches.

--- a/CMakeLists.txt	2026-05-26 09:10:23.925423526 +0200
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt	2026-05-26 09:10:23.929423596 +0200
@@ -1,6 +1,13 @@
 # CMake build script for ZeroMQ
 project(ZeroMQ)
 
+# Match GUIX cross-compile behavior: GUIX builds bitcoin via a
+# cross-toolchain even on native x86_64 (make-bitcoin-cross-toolchain),
+# so CMAKE_CROSSCOMPILING is TRUE in their build. Force it here so
+# the EFD_CLOEXEC check (line 545) and the SOCK_CLOEXEC/TCP_KEEP*/
+# TIPC/etc. check block (line 738) are skipped — matches upstream.
+set(CMAKE_CROSSCOMPILING TRUE)
+
 if(${CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME} STREQUAL Darwin)
   cmake_minimum_required(VERSION 3.0.2)
 else()
@@ -1208,6 +1215,7 @@
   list(APPEND cxx-sources vmci_address.cpp vmci_connecter.cpp vmci_listener.cpp vmci.cpp)
 endif()
 
+set(ZMQ_HAVE_TIPC FALSE)
 if(ZMQ_HAVE_TIPC)
   list(APPEND cxx-sources tipc_address.cpp tipc_connecter.cpp tipc_listener.cpp)
 endif()
